.Dd November 16, 2026
.Dt GREP 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm grep
.Nd select lines matching a pattern
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl i
.Op Fl v
.Op Fl n
.Op Fl l
.Op Fl q
.Op Fl c
.Op Fl E
.Op Fl F
.Ar pattern
.Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility selects lines in each
.Ar file
that match
.Ar pattern.
The target image currently requires at least one file; the host byte-stream core also covers
standard input.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c
Print the count of selected lines.
.It Fl E
Use extended regular expressions.
.It Fl F
Use fixed strings instead of regular expressions.
.It Fl i
Ignore case.
.It Fl l
Print only the names of matching files.
.It Fl n
Prefix each selected line with its line number.
.It Fl q
Quiet; exit 0 on the first match.
.It Fl v
Select non-matching lines.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
0 for a match, 1 for no match, 2 for usage, an invalid pattern or an I/O error.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cmp 1 ,
.Xr diff 1
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD.
